IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `fa-dispositions`

-- Factors Act 1889, ss 1 to 12 -- worked cases.
--
-- Every assertion is a claim about the ENCODING on stated facts, not about the law. Nothing here has been checked
-- against a decided case or subsidiary legislation (none was retrieved).
--
-- Fixtures are generated from a table of which flags are set (scratchpad gen_factors-act-1889.py). Expected results were written by
-- hand from the text.

`a dealer sells a consigned car to a shopper` MEANS Disposition WITH
    `the agent is a mercantile agent` IS TRUE
    `made by the agent or an authorised clerk` IS TRUE
    `the agent had actual custody` IS TRUE
    `another held the goods for the agent` IS FALSE
    `there is evidence the owner did not consent` IS FALSE
    `the documents came from consented possession` IS FALSE
    `the owner's consent had ended` IS FALSE
    `in the ordinary course of business` IS TRUE
    `the taker acted in good faith` IS TRUE
    `the taker had notice of no authority` IS FALSE
    `the taker had notice consent had ended` IS FALSE

`a dealer sells a car held in a third party's yard` MEANS Disposition WITH
    `the agent is a mercantile agent` IS TRUE
    `made by the agent or an authorised clerk` IS TRUE
    `the agent had actual custody` IS FALSE
    `another held the goods for the agent` IS TRUE
    `there is evidence the owner did not consent` IS FALSE
    `the documents came from consented possession` IS FALSE
    `the owner's consent had ended` IS FALSE
    `in the ordinary course of business` IS TRUE
    `the taker acted in good faith` IS TRUE
    `the taker had notice of no authority` IS FALSE
    `the taker had notice consent had ended` IS FALSE

